*> Implementation test (US15; docs/protocol/19-mobs-land-friendly-and-neutral.md section 10, constants): a goat takes 10 less fall damage.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-19-10-GOAT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-KEY                PIC X(24).
 01 WS-DAMAGE             BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "goat" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 15 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "M182-FALL-ADJUST" USING WS-KEY WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§10 Goat: a fall of 15 points of damage costs a goat 5 (GOAT_FALL_DAMAGE_REDUCTION 10)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DAMAGE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 4 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "M182-FALL-ADJUST" USING WS-KEY WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§10 Goat: a small fall costs a goat nothing (never below 0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DAMAGE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "sheep" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 15 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "M182-FALL-ADJUST" USING WS-KEY WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§10 Goat: another species keeps its fall damage" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 15 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DAMAGE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "frog" TO WS-KEY
     MOVE 15 TO WS-DAMAGE
     CALL "M182-FALL-ADJUST" USING WS-KEY WS-DAMAGE
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§11.1 Frog: a frog takes 5 less fall damage (FROG_FALL_DAMAGE_REDUCTION 5)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 10 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DAMAGE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-19-10-GOAT.
